        "text": "Second check-in after: 25 minutes",
        "text_sha256": "36edac5fde70d7eaab474c79c4d5849fa26739c8b57e21303893b7887de85eb8",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000061",
        "block_index": 61,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Third check-in after: 30 minutes",
        "text_sha256": "5177540a9eea64306494b4ae1436a43cbba6ec5e38e7a23ab3f78a9a8f951b32",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000062",
        "block_index": 62,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Subsequent check-in after: 30 minutes",
        "text_sha256": "4f89c9a74abfa4e0bd5e50827d1e6d3bab345612f2ad9c682723725a3e4895ce",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000063",
        "block_index": 63,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's a Ferber method chart that's easy to check and refer to:",
        "text_sha256": "7e78b97b434e3a100b9ce1d76b0861552614681efa9c6427c10dbb246bb66fa6",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000064",
        "block_index": 64,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "ferber method sleep training chart",
        "text_sha256": "3cb1a0a78e723f5d54883929be40cdd7f39ba680eca7b6125da0802c5ce9562b",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000065",
        "block_index": 65,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Do you have to follow these times exactly in order for the training to work? Having predetermined check-in times can help ensure that you’re consistent and gradually encourage your baby to do more of the work of soothing herself.",
        "text_sha256": "f3ff4379a19fd6c66888784d10e34a453da37445bf18ad05f65a572ac412bcd9",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000066",
        "block_index": 66,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But it’s okay to alter the intervals a little bit if you think something else would work better for you and your baby. The key is sticking with any changes you make. As long as you’re consistent, you should see sleep training success.",
        "text_sha256": "cb8167af9450a959719d3194d23a779cbde28b05fbe327429ec10bdac8168466",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000067",
        "block_index": 67,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How long does the Ferber sleep method take to work on your baby?",
        "text_sha256": "b9d0045986d3c0defbd0a96c365c4788e2d0ea98d18334613f3a76d67eafe433",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000068",
        "block_index": 68,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "All babies respond to sleep training in their own way, and some take to the new bedtime routine a little faster than others. But in general, you can expect the crying to diminish steadily over three nights or so. And sometime between nights four and seven, it will likely stop altogether. (Hooray!)",
        "text_sha256": "d6e3e32887eb35707c84ba5daefb6a8f639fc55c93c1fed1641aa7a54929e398",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000069",
        "block_index": 69,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Does that mean your baby will never cry at bedtime or wake up in the middle of the night again? Even after sleep training, it’s normal for your little one to hit the occasional rough patch — like when she’s sick, teething or even working on a big developmental milestone .",
        "text_sha256": "fd83b7ba39bcf7ff2eead5581d94dfc3d419512a340984a21b924494d2e620ad",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000070",
        "block_index": 70,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But now that sleep training has given her a solid foundation, it should be relatively easy for her to get back to her usual snooze routine once the issue has passed.",
        "text_sha256": "771be117fd93ba17c423e426bd710508ff4d613683528a04354e4f070f95de81",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000071",
        "block_index": 71,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Ferber sleep method training tips",
        "text_sha256": "ab17e5d0e7eed19ea8e52a41ff6fe0c65a88b360ac14109320c4a527ea6845a1",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000072",
        "block_index": 72,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The sleep training process isn’t exactly fun, but it doesn’t have to be a nightmare either.",
        "text_sha256": "4ccb611c6714d18025514933060c4d3a47dc128a2b17dc20b94e45cef64335b2",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000073",
        "block_index": 73,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "To set the stage for success — and maybe have everyone sleeping blissfully through the night a little sooner — keep these strategies in mind.",
        "text_sha256": "83b117bcf62da10b66cc1a22ba0d14137bc1d5de03e8a6392555d04bfb3074d4",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000074",
        "block_index": 74,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Be smart about your start time. Sleep training can be a big deal for both you and your baby, so block out time on the calendar when everything else is relatively calm. If your little one is sick or teething, or if you’ve got a new babysitter starting or you’re going back to work, it’s worth holding off until things have settled back down. Avoid sleep training on vacation too — travel will only derail your efforts.",
        "text_sha256": "d9de37ebbbaed470ce360f24e92bacf879327d22a752cf7897e4fc5a91bce804",
        "word_count": 77
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000075",
        "block_index": 75,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Wean nighttime feedings. It can be harder for your baby to get the hang of sleep training if you sometimes respond to her cries by going in to feed her.",
        "text_sha256": "41229da4563faf6f6345abcff25540b4d5b6da89b8096572ac2b3475dd26f23d",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000076",
        "block_index": 76,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Establish a bedtime routine, if you haven’t already. Soothing activities like a bath, book and snuggles will help your baby wind down for the night. If your bedtime routine currently ends with a feeding, try moving it earlier so there’s no risk of your baby falling asleep at the breast or bottle. Remember, she should be drowsy but awake when you put her in the crib.",
        "text_sha256": "cfa26a5f2626decc5c4b95b4a06e1a5058993a757be52dd7f98208bb994b4155",
        "word_count": 66
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000077",
        "block_index": 77,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Watch for your baby’s sleepy cues. You want to get your baby into bed when she’s nice and tired — but not overtired. Your little one will have a harder time settling down once she’s past the point of exhaustion. And she might be more likely to sleep restlessly and wake throughout the night .",
        "text_sha256": "18b157ddabc87047df0e574a9231ab6c6f15d9fb4940a790168fd85646cc7643",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000078",
        "block_index": 78,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Stick with the crib for bedtime and naps. At night, the crib is the most obvious place for sleep. But if your baby is in the habit of napping in places other than her crib, she might have a harder time sleeping well in it at night too.",
        "text_sha256": "1ee0f0fd0687e162fbc25afcce9b68d42feb98a11c8f9563404745d667dedb51",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000079",
        "block_index": 79,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Make sure both parents are on board, and consider having your partner handle check-ins. It's important that both you and your partner agree to try the Ferber method of sleep training, as you'll need each other for support during the process. And if your baby associates you with feeding and comfort, having a partner go in might help her settle down a little easier.",
        "text_sha256": "11aa6580ec6c6a1b39aeb2589059d7d742683674ab76e253b88d46375a5607f4",
        "word_count": 64
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000080",
        "block_index": 80,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Be consistent. Listening to your baby cry can be hard, and it might even tempt you to abandon your plan. But sticking with it will help her get the hang of things faster — so you all can rest easier.",
        "text_sha256": "aa68c1483ad5f30df60e9fead4b93056d5f29495b73795e6bdea3211607b8fae",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000081",
        "block_index": 81,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When to stop trying the Ferber method",
        "text_sha256": "1c3c9bb8549d6bb497430b36c68e84aded5a6483fe293cb1b57eaef2611edb62",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000082",
        "block_index": 82,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Cry it out methods like the Ferber method can be a great tool for helping babies become great sleepers. But if after a week or two, your baby hasn’t made much progress or it seems like she’s still crying a lot , it might be time to take a break.",
        "text_sha256": "011faf59383a8d5143ef78b3c950171e36fcc81fad13e7e3e7dc8854b32ec9c1",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000083",
        "block_index": 83,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You could try the Ferber method again a little later on, or switch gears and try another sleep training approach.",
        "text_sha256": "64e007c7a6099b98b385b6e7370b2e586c4d1a3a4c0aba4899fbef56bc748a6a",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000084",
        "block_index": 84,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It’s also worth talking with your baby’s pediatrician. He or she can help rule out any underlying issues that might be making it harder for your baby to sleep, like infant acid reflux , teething or an ear infection.",
        "text_sha256": "d24dd35c074a89dc1518197fc856bf373dfe6b822cb628878886d5e52270a0ed",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000085",
        "block_index": 85,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The Ferber method of sleep training can help your baby learn how to fall asleep on her own and soothe herself back to sleep when she wakes during the night. As with most sleep training approaches, there will probably be some tears.",
        "text_sha256": "42ffe83ca31de0645a8486af5d417c061efcb85774197f81f0074f139e57eb33",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000086",
        "block_index": 86,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But if you’re consistent, the crying will decrease after just a few days. And within a week or two she — and you — will be getting a better night’s sleep.",
        "text_sha256": "c943e869ae6fd657eda12dd9595f2c1114a6ec86e7ce554994b2fa6686ea0017",
        "word_count": 31
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 1774,
    "heading_count": 16
  },
  "title": "What Is the Ferber Method of Sleep Training?",
